      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{642b3036ffd38909cda88cd4|full_name} \n\nIs it set to 6 months for end users? Did that change since groups came out? When I made this post a year ago, it seemed like the retention period was just 1 month. If it really is 6 months now, that is actually a major improvement. 1 Month is/was just too low.\n\nAnd an `acceptedBy` field would be great. In certain group contexts this is equivalent to their \"sponsor\" or the person who vouches for them. And this is very useful for tracking down who is adding certain people to the group if trouble crops up.\n\nModeration tools for end users need more information, not less. Especially if the goal is to offload moderation to the community and to treat it as another piece of UGC. \n\nAnd I do recognize that there are limitations to how much can be offered before the information can be used for harassment. My sentiment exists within a reasonable interpretation of those bounds.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
